Let's find a recursive formula for $f(n)$.

- The first term is the number of bear in the first year, which is $\blue{1000}$ bears.
- The common ratio is the factor by which the number of bears multiplied each year, which is $\pink{0.90}$.

Therefore, this is the recursive definition of the sequence:

$\begin{cases}
f(1)=\blue{1000}
\\\\
f(n)=f(n-1)\cdot\pink{0.9}
\end{cases}$

In conclusion, $f$ is a *geometric* sequence.

$\begin{cases}
f(1)=\blue{1000}
\\\\
f(n)=f(n-1)\cdot\pink{0.9}
\end{cases}$
